    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1290">

                <pb facs="1026" n="910" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg910"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/6.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at
                            Chihuahua to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-24T15:00:00-07:04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1912—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador advised me by telegraph yesterday that Mexican Government will not
                    attempt second collection of taxes paid rebel authorities, and he has instructed
                    advising Americans to this effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
